  "label": "User projected onto the subordinate Nazi official as 'loser'",
  "description": "The user is projected onto the man standing outside the car (a Nazi official) who is being mocked by the text 'get in loser'. The meme uses this visual and textual material to imply that the user is being forced to participate in a morally reprehensible act (invasion of Poland), thereby equating the user with the subordinate in the image. This projection is implicit through the deictic 'loser' applied to the subordinate, which the user identifies with as a target of ridicule.",
